HST Office: the Insert › Symbol drop-down offers check boxes, ticks, arrows and the common signs.

The drop-down shows the favourite and the recent characters. Upstream's defaults are twelve favourites (€ ¥ £ © Σ Ω
≤ ≥ ∞ π † ‡) and no recent ones, so the symbols Word users pick from its Symbol gallery every day (☐ ☑ ☒ ✓ ✔ ✗,
arrows, ± × ÷, ₫, №) were only in the Special Character dialog. The favourites are now ☐ ☑ ☒ ✓ ✔ ✗ • → ⇒ ° ± ×
(twelve, so four of the sixteen places stay free for the user's own), and the recent list starts like Word's gallery
with ≤ ≥ ≠ ≈ ∞ ÷ ← ↑ ↓ € © ₫ №, which the user's own picks then push out as before. All are Unicode characters
(no Wingdings code points). Box and tick glyphs use DejaVu Sans, which HST bundles on every platform and which has
all of them; the others use Times New Roman, HST Writer's default font (Liberation Serif stands in on Linux).
Profiles that already changed either list keep theirs.

